# IPaging and Paging

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Persistence`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Persistence.Core`
**Version**: 0.6.0

## Purpose

Paging types used by `IStore<T>.FindManyAsync` to specify a result window.

## `IPaging`

```csharp
public interface IPaging
{
    int Skip { get; }
    int Take { get; }
}
```

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `Skip` | `int` | Number of items to skip from the start of the result set. |
| `Take` | `int` | Number of items to take (page size). |

## `Paging`

```csharp
public class Paging : IPaging
{
    public Paging(int skip, int take);
    public int Skip { get; }
    public int Take { get; }

    public static Paging Page(int page, int pageSize) => new(page * pageSize, pageSize);
    public static Paging? Create(int? skip, int? take) => skip != null && take != null ? new Paging(skip.Value, take.Value) : default;
}
```

| Member | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `Paging(int skip, int take)` | Constructor with explicit skip/take. |
| `Skip` / `Take` | Read-only properties. |
| `Page(int page, int pageSize)` | Static factory: returns `new Paging(page * pageSize, pageSize)`. |
| `Create(int? skip, int? take)` | Static factory: returns `new Paging(skip, take)` only if both inputs are non-null; otherwise returns `default` (i.e. `null`). |

## Usage Example

```csharp
// Page-based (page 2, 10 items per page)
var data = await store.FindManyAsync(
    new AllSpecification<MyData>(),
    paging: Paging.Page(page: 2, pageSize: 10));

// Skip/take-based with nullable input
int? skip = 20, take = 5;
var paged = Paging.Create(skip, take);
```

## Related
- `IStore<T>.FindManyAsync` — Consumes `IPaging?` as the paging parameter
- `StoreExtensions.FindManyAsync` — Lambda overload that also accepts `Paging?`
